# clangd, for the C runtime.
#
# The flags themselves are in `runtime/c/compile_flags.txt`, because clangd
# resolves a relative `-I` there against that file's own directory -- which is
# what makes `#include "nts_runtime.h"` resolve from both `runtime/c` and
# `runtime/c/tests`. Without it clangd has no flags at all and reports the
# header as missing and `bool` as an unknown type, which is noise that trains
# you to ignore the gutter.
#
# `-DNTS_PROVIDER_RC` is a choice, not a default. The runtime compiles under two
# memory providers and clangd can only see one; reference counting is the one
# with `nts_free`, the cycle collector and the retain/release paths in it, so it
# is the half worth having analysed. The NoGC build is covered by the gate.

# Check selection lives in `.clang-tidy`, which clang-tidy on the command line
# reads too -- so the editor gutter and a terminal run cannot disagree.
Diagnostics:
  UnusedIncludes: Strict
